atomy-toolkit
=============

This product includes ported engineering-discipline skills derived from:

  addyosmani/agent-skills  (https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills)
  Copyright (c) Addy Osmani and the agent-skills contributors.
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The 16 Korean-language rewrites of addyosmani/agent-skills workflows that
previously shipped as cascade skills were removed in 2026-08 (productization
cleanroom review): their subject matter (WCAG, OpenTelemetry, Core Web Vitals,
CI/CD gating) targets professional developers, while this toolkit's primary
users are non-developers. They remain retrievable from git history.

Additionally, OWASP Top 10 coverage (security-check) and 5-axis review guidance
(review) absorb material from addyosmani/agent-skills security-and-hardening and
code-review-and-quality.

Optional dependency
-------------------

The `graph` extra (`pip install atomy-toolkit-lib[graph]`) installs:

  graphifyy  (https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Safi Shamsi.
  Licensed under the MIT License.

It is not installed by default and no graphify source is vendored here; the
extra declares a PyPI requirement only. `/plandoc` degrades to a stdlib-`ast`
lite mode when it is absent.

